/-! Exact support-profile comparison operators based on v17, pp. 51--55.
Nine low coefficients are enlarged to dominate the checked predecessor caps;
Certificate.lean checks the exact old_low trajectory
through its finite prefix and invariant, and LowTransfer checks cap domination.
The startup vector is enlarged to reuse the checked older five-degree smoothing
bounds. Its u1--u4 prefix is the exact rational recurrence trajectory
for the enlarged low map.
All finite prefix comparisons are checked by Certificate.lean.
These internal vectors belong to the historical 2^(-92-41*k) target.
They do not certify the current paper's 7*2^(-95-41*k) theorem.
All decimals are represented by rational expressions. Coordinates are ordered
(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(0,4),(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(2,2),(2,3),(2,4),(3,3),(3,4),(4,4).
These are sufficient comparison operators; no AES estimate is asserted here.
-/
